      "text": "Hi there, how are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 10.65,
      "end": 20.1,
      "text": "No problem. Park on flat ground, and wait until the engine's been off for a few minutes. Then open the bonnet and look for a handle with a loop, usually yellow or orange."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 23.03,
      "end": 29.95,
      "text": "Yes. Wipe it clean, push it all the way back in, then pull it out again. The oil should sit between the two marks near the tip."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 35.29,
      "end": 42.717,
      "text": "Then it's worth topping up a little. Your manual will tell you the right oil type. Add a small amount at a time and recheck, you don't want to overfill."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 47.407,
      "end": 52.647,
      "text": "Once a month is a good habit, and before any long drive. You're already ahead of most new drivers."
